CORE
main.py
--unwind 5
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
--
PLR 8.4: a call that raises inside an expression stops the rest of its
statement -- the enclosing call (`note(f(1))`), the branch an if condition
selects, the rest of a short-circuit expression. goto-convert lifts the call
out of the expression; a goto-level pass jumps to the end of the Python
statement right after it (python_exception_instrumentation).
